# The minisign public keys that sign CodeSmith releases. `codesmith upgrade`
# (compiled in with include_str!) and install.sh (RELEASE_KEYS, which a test
# keeps equal to this list) trust a release whose SHA256SUMS.minisig verifies
# with any key listed here. See "Signing the checksums" in RELEASING.md.
#
# One key per line: the second line of the key's .pub file (56 characters,
# starting with RW). Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. List
# two keys while rotating from one to the next.
#
# The CodeSmith release key: ~/.minisign/codesmith.pub on Skeptic-Mac, the
# Mac that holds its secret key (~/.minisign/codesmith.key) and signs every
# release's SHA256SUMS with scripts/sign-release.sh. A file holding only the
# line PLACEHOLDER (no key) makes upgrades check SHA256SUMS only; one with
# neither a key nor PLACEHOLDER refuses upgrades.
RWTFKe6qhvSs57s1pw5x6aJRK0jdZr42tg1NgNp3a9rAJ3HersFsRoMV
